<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Hardened-runtime entitlements for the app bundle and its main executable.

  Keep this set minimal: every key here weakens a protection of the main,
  unsandboxed process that handles untrusted network input.

  The app is intentionally NOT App-Sandboxed (torrenting's listening ports and
  arbitrary user-folder writes fight the sandbox), so network client/server
  access needs no entitlement. Library validation stays ON: build_app.sh signs
  the vendored dylibs (libtorrent/OpenSSL/libssh2) and Sparkle with the same
  identity as the app, so they share its Team ID and load without
  disable-library-validation.

  * automation.apple-events — "shut down / sleep when downloads finish" asks
    System Events via NSAppleScript (GoelApp/LiveSystemActions.swift). Under the
    hardened runtime an Apple event is refused without this key, even when the
    user has approved Goel° in Privacy & Security → Automation. It pairs with
    NSAppleEventsUsageDescription in Info.plist.

  The yt-dlp helper needs JIT, unsigned executable memory and disabled library
  validation for its PyInstaller-frozen Python. Those live in YtDlp.entitlements
  and are applied to that one binary only — never add them here.

  Check a signed build by passing codesign's display flag plus its
  entitlements flag (value "-") for dist/Goel°.app and for
  Contents/Resources/yt-dlp; build_app.sh runs that check itself. (A double
  hyphen is illegal inside an XML comment, and AMFI's parser rejects it.)
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.automation.apple-events</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
